\begin{cases} 2x + 4y = 40 \\ x + y = 15 \end{cases}
\] Solving this system of equations, we can find the values of $x$ and $y$. First, simplify the first equation by dividing everything by 2: \[ x + 2y = 20 \] Now we have the simplified system: \[ \begin{cases} x + 2y = 20 \\ x + y = 15 \end{cases} \] Subtract the second equation from the first equation to eliminate $x$: \[ (x + 2y) - (x + y) = 20 - 15 \] This simplifies to: \[ y = 5 \] Substitute $y = 5$ into the second equation: \[ x + 5 = 15 \] Solving for $x$, we get: \[ x = 10 \] So the number of acrobats is 10. </think> <answer> 10 </answer>

