\begin{cases} 
2x + 4y = 40 & \text{(since acrobats have 2 legs and elephants have 4 legs)} \\ 
x + y = 15 & \text{(since each acrobat and elephant has 1 head)} 
\end{cases}
\] Solving the second equation for $x$, we get $x = 15 - y$. Substituting this into the first equation, we get $2(15 - y) + 4y = 40$. Simplifying, we get $30 - 2y + 4y = 40$, which leads to $2y = 10$, so $y = 5$. Substituting $y = 5$ back into the equation $x = 15 - y$, we get $x = 10$. Therefore, the number of acrobats is 10.</think> <answer> 10 </answer>

